//
// Conduit (--use-conduit --conduit-fuse-spatial) end-to-end run for
// `--conduit-fuse-operators` 1:1 spatial fusion (basic).  E2E companion to
// lit-only pin
//   test/Dialect/Conduit/fuse_operators_basic.mlir
// and Python-harness sibling
//   iron_operator_mlir/fusion_npu_regression/fuse_operators_smoke.py.
//
// Pre-fuse: 2 separate `aie.device` blocks (devAdd + devMul), each at
// tile(0,2) of column 0.  After `--conduit-fuse-spatial` (which injects
// `--conduit-fuse-operators` per `aiecc.cpp:332`) the two devices collapse
// into ONE merged device with devMul's tiles offset to column 1 — so the
// merged producer core sits at tile(0,2) and the merged consumer core at
// tile(1,2).  The intermediate conduit pair (`@inter_add` / `@consume_add`,
// both tagged `fusion_group="addmul_smoke_op"`) is replaced by a single
// `@fused_intermediate_0` cross-column on-chip channel.  Two-column smoke
// uses `npu2_2col`.
//
// Spatial-only (NO `--conduit-fuse-core-bodies-flag`): `--aie-combine-
// device same-tile=false` is the default routing without the core-bodies
// flag, so the two cores do NOT collapse onto one tile; they spread across
// columns 0 and 1.  The merged-device on-chip routing for the surviving
// fused_intermediate channel must be correct for the dispatch to succeed
// — that is what this smoke validates.
//
// PASS expectation: every dispatch (4 invocations) completes; output
// bytes match reference computed by test.cpp (out[j] = (in[j]+1.0)*2.0,
// in[j] = (j%16)).  Failure modes that lit-only fixtures cannot catch
// (per fuse_operators_smoke.py docstring):
//   * Spatial fusion produces compile-clean IR but the merged-device ELF
//     deadlocks or misroutes on hardware (Bug A/B regression class).  Lit
//     verifies IR shape only — it cannot observe hardware-level routing
//     correctness or ELF dispatch behavior.
//   * `arg_index`-driven channel-merge silently drops an output buffer
//     slot (#77 / #78 regression class).  IR may still verify, but the
//     dropped slot leaves the host-visible output BO unwritten or
//     corrupted; only an end-to-end byte check surfaces this.
//   * Trim-after-merge corrupts host ABI (#99) — caught by all-zero
//     output observation that lit-only validation cannot see.  When the
//     intermediate-erase step trims the runtime sequence's arg list and
//     mis-aligns surviving args to BO bindings, the kernel writes nothing
//     observable to bo_out and every byte stays at the pre-dispatch
//     `memset(0)` value.
//
// Sibling references:
//   * `test/npu-xrt/fuse_operators_convergent_npu/conduit.lit` — same
//     pipeline (`--conduit-fuse-spatial`) at K=2 convergent shape; this
//     fixture is the K=1 (1:1) baseline that convergent extends.
//   * `test/npu-xrt/fuse_core_bodies_npu/conduit.lit` — same Add → Mul
//     1:1 chain at the IR level, but with the hybrid pipeline
//     (`--conduit-fuse-core-bodies-flag --conduit-fuse-spatial`) that
//     additionally collapses both cores onto one tile via
//     `--aie-combine-device same-tile=true`.  Diffing the two fixtures'
//     post-compile IR isolates which behavior is contributed by spatial
//     vs. core-bodies fusion.
//   * `test/Dialect/Conduit/fuse_operators_basic.mlir` — canonical lit-
//     only pin for `--conduit-fuse-operators` 1:1 (CHECK lines for IR
//     shape: cross-column tile offset, `@fused_intermediate_0` rename,
//     external I/O survival).
//
// No stateful companion: the source IR uses 2 independent `aie.device`
// blocks linked only by `fusion_group` annotations — stateful objectfifo
// lowering does not span devices, so a stateful run is structurally
// inapplicable here.  Reference is computed in test.cpp.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai, peano
//
// Kernel compute is inlined bf16 add + multiply.  Chess (xchesscc) cannot
// select `fp_to_bf16` for this inline core (`fatal error: error in
// backend: Cannot select: i32 = fp_to_bf16`); Peano can.  Use
// `--no-xchesscc --no-xbridge` to route the kernel compile through Peano
// (sibling pattern: `convergent_npu/conduit.lit`,
// `fuse_core_bodies_npu/conduit.lit`, `loadpdi/run.lit`,
// `vec_vec_add_objfifo_init/aie2.py`).
//
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2_2col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python aiecc.py --no-aiesim --no-xchesscc --no-xbridge --aie-generate-xclbin --aie-generate-npu-insts --no-compile-host --use-conduit --conduit-fuse-spatial --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% clang %S/test.cpp -o test.exe -std=c++17 -Wall %xrt_flags -lrt -lstdc++ %test_utils_flags
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
